# tools/m/mantra_spool_dedup_ratio_witness.rish -- the spool-scale dedup ratio the
# fourth angle named and left untouched.
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES. mantra/spool.rye winds a large artifact across ordered resins, each
# split at a fixed, absolute byte offset (beading.max_resin_bytes), and beads every
# resin with the fixed-size beading.bead alone -- it never calls
# beading.bead_content_defined. mantra/spool_dedup_ratio.rye measures what an insert or
# delete costs under that fixed-offset split: every resin boundary at or past the edit
# now falls on different bytes than before, so a shift's cost depends on how much of
# the artifact lies downstream of it rather than on the edit's own size. This guard
# proves the binary still compiles, still reaches its own closing line, and still
# reports the two bucket readings the scan's own header names.
#
# WHAT IT FOUND, recorded here so a reader comparing this guard against a later run
# knows what changed if the numbers move. Same-length SUBSTITUTE edits dedup at 750-875
# permille regardless of position or size (6 configs, mean 833 permille) -- the resin
# split never moves, so only the touched resin's own beads cost anything. INSERT and
# DELETE collapse to ZERO permille when planted early in the artifact (2 of 6 shifting
# configs), where nearly everything lies downstream of the edit and every downstream
# resin re-chunks into different bytes; the same edit shapes recover toward the
# substitute floor the later they land, since less of the artifact remains downstream.
#
# This guard reads the two bucket readings rather than pinning every row: a reader
# wanting the full position-by-position picture runs the scan and reads the twelve
# `config ...` lines fresh. What this guard DOES pin is structural -- that the shifting
# bucket genuinely reaches zero somewhere in the sweep, which is the reading that
# confirms a fixed-offset split pays the cost beading.rye's own content-defined chunker
# exists to avoid, and that the substitute bucket stays well clear of zero, which
# confirms the position-independence a same-length edit is supposed to have.
#
# Full research writeup:
#   active-designing/date/20261001/20261001-184131_the-one-real-revision-this-tree-has-is-a-shift.md
#   active-designing/date/20261001/20261001-182131_the-ratio-the-comment-was-actually-about.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mantra_spool_dedup_ratio_witness.rish

say "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: Language EN -- reading what a shift costs when the resin split itself sits at a fixed byte offset."
say "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: Style Gauge, Meter -- every claim is a count the built binary printed."
say "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: Lens TAME -- a measurement this tree can rerun rather than a number taken on faith."

say "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: building and running the synthetic sweep..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/m/mantra_spool_dedup_ratio_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: the scan must complete"
assert scan.out contains "built=yes" else "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: the binary did not compile, so every reading below is a reading of nothing"
assert scan.out contains "configs=12" else "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: the sweep's own config count moved -- read the new figure before trusting any bucket beside it"

say "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: same-length substitutions must stay well clear of zero -- a fixed-offset split pays no cost when nothing shifts..."
assert scan.out contains "substitute_mean_ratio_pm=833 of 6 configs" else "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: the substitute bucket moved -- re-read the scan's own header before trusting this line again"

say "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: at least one shifting config must read near zero -- the cost a fixed-offset resin split cannot resync away..."
assert scan.out contains "shifting_near_zero=2 of 6 configs" else "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: the shifting bucket moved -- re-read the scan's own header before trusting this line again"

assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "mantra-spool-dedup-ratio: the scan reached its own red"

say "GREEN: a same-length substitute costs a spool almost nothing (833 permille mean); an early insert or delete costs it everything downstream (0 permille), and the cost recovers toward the substitute floor the later the edit lands."
